WEBVTT

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.740
What is this?

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:20.910
It couldn't be...

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.950
An M.J.B.K.?

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:34.900
At one time, man was one with the world of truth.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:40.270
But the written word brought forth prosperity and suffering.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:49.480
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:55.480
<i>The kanji for "love" and "grief " look very similar</i>

00:00:55.480 --> 00:01:00.890
<i>When I realized that, dawn suddenly broke</i>

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:06.660
<i>The air was filled with so much</i> <i>silence that "blue" "fought"</i>

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:13.000
<i>When suddenly you slid in to the right of me</i>

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.910
<i>Rippling with a clatter</i>

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:18.840
<i>and tangled in red thread</i>

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:23.750
<i>and a 39-degree fever of passion</i>

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:29.190
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:35.260
<i>A crown worn on high with pride</i>

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:40.700
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>"soothe" my hidden "heart below"</i>

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:46.700
<i>Its form is too much to handle right now</i>

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:49.640
<i>God's wisdom, the "h" in "her"</i>

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:52.370
<i>With a tearful, feverish gaze</i>

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:55.310
<i>let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon</i>

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:58.150
<i>(Let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon)</i>

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:05.550
<i>The things you can do are so striking</i>

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:14.990
"Clear Them! The Inviting Shadows"

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.830
No way.

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:10.010
Even my supposedly M.J.B.K.-proof
Aquariphone isn't working.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.860
There's no doubt about it.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:18.120
This is a fake world created by the M.J.B.K.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.470
Shirobaco?

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.610
Master Sougon?

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:41.610
What path should I be taking?

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:48.390
The one with the flame M.J.B.K. was the son of Nesta's CEO,

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:51.430
Subete Kenzaki, correct?

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:53.330
And when we first fought,

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:57.300
you were together with him aboard that black Aquarion, right?

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.830
It's the manager!

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:02.440
You and Subete were comrades who trained together.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:03.740
Is that right?

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:06.740
Comrades? I'm not sure.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:11.480
I was only with him because that was my duty.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:14.450
That's me... Why?

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:16.190
Who ordered you to?

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:19.690
Master Sougon. Sougon Kenzaki.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:20.790
Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:23.430
Be more gentle, would you?

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:24.990
I'm being plenty gentle.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:28.460
Half of me is made up of gentleness!

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:30.500
And the other half's what? Boobies?

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:32.470
Let me tighten those bandages for you.

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:34.340
Ouch! Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.210
I was joking! Just joking, okay?

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.680
"A Flame War Strikes in Midsummer Tokyo"

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:42.780
This was right after we fought the flame M.J.B.K.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:46.220
I remember talking with the commander...

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.650
Your duty, huh?

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:51.220
In order to bring out the Vector's potential,

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:54.860
two people with Verbalism ability needed to Gattai.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:59.120
Subete and I were partners for that. That's all.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:04.870
Yes. That's all there should have been to my relationship with Subete.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:07.200
Maia. Hey, Maia.

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:10.730
So, why?

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:14.740
Maia, you listening?

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:17.850
You free after this? Let's go grab a bite to eat!

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.380
Return to your room.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.380
Let's go eat chiffon cake!

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.880
Chiffon cake is so sweet and delicious!

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:29.930
It really is sweet! Come on, Maia.
Let's go for sure next time.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.600
Maia!

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.570
Do you know what a planetarium is?

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:42.940
They set one up in the facility downstairs.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.430
Time to go.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:53.580
Why? Why does Subete try to get involved with me, I wonder?

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.850
Why?

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:58.220
Why are you doing that?

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:04.460
Huh? Why are you here, Maia?

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:08.960
The Verbalism Ability resonance test was supposed to start a while ago.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:13.300
Everyone else is busy setting up, so I was told to come get you.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:15.040
By Dad?

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:16.640
By Master Sougon.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:20.910
That right? Dad sure does talk to you a lot.

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:23.240
He won't even spare a glance in my direction.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:29.120
Why are you doing that?

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:33.650
I don't need them anymore.
These things are useless to me.

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:43.300
Hey, what do you think I'd have to do to please Dad?

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.830
Should I train harder?

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:48.900
Or should I try baseball because soccer's not working out?

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:51.570
Hey, what do you think I should do?

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:56.110
Come on, tell me.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:04.020
It'll be okay.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.960
I'm sure you can get stronger.

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:17.290
This is when Subete started trying to be around me more than necessary.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:23.340
Back then, I thought Subete was capable of becoming stronger.

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:28.330
I wanted him to become stronger. Why?

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:44.290
This is my first memory...
My memory of how I met Subete...

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:59.230
That's right. I was saved. By Subete.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:05.480
Subete said he was going to take you back.

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:08.380
That he needed you as his partner, so he would take you back.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:10.650
Though it looked like there was more to it than that.

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:13.060
What are you trying to say?

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:14.690
You know, the thing about people is...

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:19.060
In the end, they act according to their emotions, not reason.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:20.930
Women especially.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:26.600
I was just a little worried about you.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:33.880
Subete is seeking me.
And I was saved by Subete.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:38.550
Then... is Subete the one
I should be living with?

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:40.040
Indeed.

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:47.120
To be with Subete.
That is what you were born for.

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:48.720
Verbalize!

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:54.390
This is the only place for you.

00:08:57.070 --> 00:09:00.240
Your face is a mess.

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:02.860
Without a will of your own, you're nothing more than a puppet.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:08.640
In the end, I can only live the way
Master Sougon sets out for me.

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:11.380
I always knew that.

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:15.420
So, why?

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:18.150
Why won't my heart take the next step?

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:19.920
That is a lie.

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:26.600
You haven't lost your path, only your bearings.

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:30.330
For there is always just one path for you to follow.

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:32.400
Who's there?

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:35.900
Yes, this has been preordained.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:39.940
I am what awakened 12,000 years ago...

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:41.970
Your fate.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:44.940
"Pearl Center"

00:09:55.490 --> 00:10:00.630
Vectors 4, 5 and 6 have been successfully activated.

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:04.500
Taking readings for all pilots' baseline vital signals.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:09.300
Vehicles and civilians are evacuated from the Asagaya Station rotary.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:12.140
Catapult lane is clear for launch.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.970
Mirage field deployed.

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:22.020
Image is locked in place.

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:24.150
--Verbalize.
--Verbalize.

00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:25.640
Verbalize.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:58.590
I've been wondering for a while now, but why do you need to train your body?

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:01.690
Are you planning to go slug it out with them or something?

00:11:01.690 --> 00:11:06.360
Well, Verbalism Ability is the power to give voice to your feelings, isn't it?

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:12.330
It can be strengthened by training your voice, but that's not the only way.

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:16.330
You can also have strong feelings.
What can you do to achieve that?

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:20.610
When an animal encounters an enemy,

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:24.080
it instinctively tries to make a judgment on if it can win.

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:26.350
Humans do the same.

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:29.790
This guy, I can beat. That guy, I can't.

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:32.590
Which leaves you with a stronger emotion?

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:35.690
The former, generally.

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:38.530
The confidence that you can dominate your opponent.

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:43.800
Ultimately, it depends on whether you can believe in your own strength or not.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:48.140
To believe in yourself, you need to be strong.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.610
This is all just stuff I learned from Dad, though.

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:54.610
I see. It's the sort of straightforward logic I'd expect from you.

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:56.650
That said, here's another thought.

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:57.710
What?

00:11:57.710 --> 00:12:01.210
The strongest is not always guaranteed to win.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:10.760
The proper choice, when faced with an opponent too powerful to fight,

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:13.560
is to give up on fighting.

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:17.730
But, on rare occasions, there are those who make the wrong choice.

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:20.240
Do you think those people are fools?

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:22.000
Yes, I do.

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:27.770
I figured you would. And you're right.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:34.620
However, never underestimate a fool who makes that mistake.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.790
The man who, armed only with the blade called confidence,

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:40.520
will face any opponent, no matter how heavily armed,

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:43.460
can be surprisingly stubborn and dangerous.

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:44.990
I don't really get it.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:48.960
If you're strong, you can win.
No matter who you face.

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:52.600
Your heart is like that glass.

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:57.370
Because it's so pure, it only shows the straight and just path.

00:12:57.370 --> 00:12:59.930
Thanks... I think?

00:13:01.610 --> 00:13:04.010
But you had best be careful.

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:07.350
The more beautiful the glass, the more easily it shatters.

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:25.630
What was that just now?

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:32.140
...aia! Maia!

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:33.700
Karan's voice?

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:38.910
Maia!

00:13:38.910 --> 00:13:43.250
Maia! I brought you the deluxe Shirobaco lunch set!

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:47.860
It's freshly made! Come out soon, or I'll eat it!

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:49.990
You think she's gonna come when you call out like that?

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:51.560
Is she a glutton character, or something?

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:53.930
Tsutomu, you quit slacking and shout, too!

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:55.660
I'll make you and your life crash if you don't!

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:56.830
Yeah, yeah.

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:58.370
There's no sign of her.

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:01.570
Hayato, you start shouting, too!

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:04.510
Wouldn't calling her politician-style with a speech be cool?

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:06.940
No. And shouting tires me out.

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:06.910
"Hayato Kujyo"

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:10.410
You don't need to shout, Big Bro.
It doesn't suit your character.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:12.550
What? That's gotta be slacking off!

00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:15.620
My concentration is focused on finding her with the sensors.

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:18.850
Having all three of us shouting wouldn't be much more effective.

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:22.120
--Hey! Maia!
--It's been eight hours since
Tsukigane and Vector-2 vanished.

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:24.890
--Come out!
--I didn't expect it to go this long without anything changing.

00:14:24.890 --> 00:14:27.900
--I'm getting sleepy!
--As soon as she entered the space,
Maia's Vector was swallowed up

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:31.430
--Yeah, well go to sleep.
And crash while you're at it.
--by the shadows, and we lost her.

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:35.070
--Hmph! You're just Tsutomu!
--She must be somewhere in that M.J.B.K. space.

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:40.140
--I managed to stay up real late on Christmas!
--The M.J.B.K. followed Tsukigane's example and its body became a shadow.

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:43.310
--Yeah, yeah, must be hard being a child idol.
--Without a physical form, there's no way to attack it.

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:45.310
What to do?

00:14:45.310 --> 00:14:48.550
At present, the M.J.B.K. has had no significant effect,

00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:52.450
and the word corrosion rate has stayed low, as well.

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:55.250
Do we just need to tough it out and be patient?

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:57.730
Where are you heading?

00:14:57.730 --> 00:14:59.230
I've rested long enough.

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:03.330
Kaibuki, you were out searching for five hours straight.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:07.400
"Hayato Kujyo"

00:15:03.330 --> 00:15:05.170
You may have been in a Vector all that time,

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:07.640
but your Verbalism Ability must be considerably drained.

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:10.170
Charging off on your own would be a bother to the rest of us.

00:15:10.170 --> 00:15:12.470
Understand that resting is part of your duties.

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:20.650
Hey, Maia! Come out!

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:32.430
So you're fine with fighting alongside us from here on, right?

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:35.630
Yep! My dream just changed from being a TV personality to being a voice actor.

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:37.830
So I still want to become famous!

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:42.200
Like we promised, once the
M.J.B.K. menace is no more,

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:45.610
we'll give your rise in the industry a strong push from behind!

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:47.340
Yippee!

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:53.440
I'm in! Sounds like we'll be fighting for justice, and that's so cool!

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:57.350
I'd rather you not make the decision so lightly...

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:59.620
So, this... Verbalism Ability, was it?

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:02.460
If I train it, it'll raise my ability to communicate with people, right?

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:04.560
That sounds awesome!

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:06.700
"Verbalism Club (Working Name)

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:06.700
Pilot Candidate"

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:06.900
Well... Yes, it is.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.800
You know, I want to conquer the world of comedy.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:11.730
If it boosts my ability to reach people,

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:14.040
it should raise my ability to make them laugh, right?

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:18.210
That brings my domination closer!
How could I not be in?

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:21.680
So, yeah, that Verbalism Club?
I'll gladly join. Thanks for having me.

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:23.410
You're welcome...

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:25.810
It changed again.

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:29.420
I... want to change Japanese politics.

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:31.420
So, you want to be a politician?

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:35.660
Then maybe you're not up for fighting on the front lines.

00:16:35.660 --> 00:16:40.490
I never said that. I'm very interested in this Verbalism Ability.

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:44.930
What is a politician's greatest weapon?

00:16:44.930 --> 00:16:46.770
Their money? Connections?

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:50.770
No. I believe it's their words.

00:16:50.770 --> 00:16:55.340
If Verbalism Ability is key to bringing out the power in words,

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:57.550
it's an ability I will need.

00:16:57.550 --> 00:16:59.610
I'll join the Verbalism Club.

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:08.120
They have things they must do in this place.

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:11.920
As do you.

00:17:13.290 --> 00:17:17.230
What I must do... Monitoring Akira...

00:17:17.230 --> 00:17:22.040
But you are different.
You have a place to return to.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:25.410
That's right. I'm here on orders.

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:28.610
Remember now.

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:30.980
I●●●

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:34.280
This is not where you truly belong.

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:39.480
"Anomalous M.J.B.K. Value Activation"

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:41.790
Gravitational abnormality in the M.J.B.K. space.

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:43.760
Propulsion units on all
Vector Machines have weakened.

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:46.730
We're detecting a rapid drop in the number of sunspots.

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:49.330
Word corrosion rate has started rising!

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:50.770
I-It's moving at an incredible rate!

00:17:50.770 --> 00:17:52.230
Why now, all of a sudden?

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:54.740
I... I'll head out, too!

00:17:54.740 --> 00:17:56.600
--What's that?
--An eclipse?

00:17:56.600 --> 00:17:58.100
Seriously?

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:04.580
What's going on? It suddenly got all dark.

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:06.410
I can't see where I'm going!

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:08.980
But we still can't see the
M.J.B.K.'s physical form.

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:11.680
Even if we Gattai, we can't do anything about it.

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:18.030
I can't see anything.

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:20.430
Where should I go?

00:18:20.430 --> 00:18:22.500
You don't have to be afraid.

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:25.990
You have someone to show you the way, don't you?

00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:31.930
Master Sougon...

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:37.480
As you always have, always will...

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:41.610
You should just follow your fate as he directs you.

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:47.720
Master Sougon.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:53.960
Answer me, Master Sougon.

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:58.990
You taught me people's happiness lies in a world without words.

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:08.510
But what do you think about the people being hurt to achieve it?

00:19:08.510 --> 00:19:13.040
Answer me! Are you really just?

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:18.920
That's dangerous! Akira!

00:19:21.020 --> 00:19:23.590
Maia Tsukigane, where are you?

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:25.990
Outsider.

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:30.870
You who are outside the ring of fate have no right to touch her.

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:32.360
Who're you?

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:38.200
Why won't you answer me, Master Sougon?

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:42.100
Master Sougon?

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:50.410
The one he sees... isn't me?

00:19:58.390 --> 00:20:01.800
I see how it was.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:06.100
You were never looking at me to begin with.

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:09.400
All along... All along...!

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:13.070
Begone, Outsider. You who lack the right.

00:20:13.070 --> 00:20:15.110
You're annoying.

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:19.210
Where should I go?

00:20:19.210 --> 00:20:21.310
What should I live for?

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:26.450
This place is dark... and cold...

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:29.120
What right do I need to save someone?

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:32.960
Save me...

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:35.990
Save me!

00:20:37.100 --> 00:20:38.590
Maia!

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:44.470
Maia!

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:46.130
A voice...

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:55.850
I can see it! The light! The world!

00:20:57.320 --> 00:20:59.650
Shadows are created by light.

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:03.090
Not the darkness of despair.

00:21:03.090 --> 00:21:08.330
I see. This voice... will always save me.

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:09.660
"Shadow"

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:10.830
"Scenery"

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:17.340
This scenery will!

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:42.300
Master Sougon, I will go with the ones who've taken my hand.

00:21:42.300 --> 00:21:47.800
If you stand in the way of that path,
I will test your intentions.

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:51.140
And if they are misguided...

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:55.870
...I will...!

00:21:59.010 --> 00:22:02.070
The M.J.B.K. has disappeared from our scanners.

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:08.320
She's such a pain.

00:22:12.690 --> 00:22:14.330
Are you okay?

00:22:14.330 --> 00:22:16.660
Yeah. It's no big deal.

00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:39.890
<i>Je-Je t'aime communication</i>

00:22:39.890 --> 00:22:49.890
<i>Oh, you aren't making a bit of</i> <i>eye contact with me while you talk</i>

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:59.140
<i>Are you texting some far-off</i> <i>neighboring world or something?</i>

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:04.270
<i>Because this isn't communication at all</i>

00:23:06.210 --> 00:23:12.750
<i>You'd at least understand that much</i>

00:23:12.750 --> 00:23:18.760
<i>even if the times suddenly changed, right?</i>

00:23:18.760 --> 00:23:22.760
<i>Give me je t'aime communication sometimes</i>

00:23:22.760 --> 00:23:26.170
<i>Look at me, answer me, and tell me</i>

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:32.670
<i>I mean, this is practically</i> <i>like talking to a computer</i>

00:23:32.670 --> 00:23:35.680
<i>A-Adieu application</i>

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:42.320
<i>Even if it means staying lonely</i> <i>in my heart, if it'll connect us</i>

00:23:42.320 --> 00:23:48.690
<i>then, please, at least show</i> <i>your smile to me alone</i>

00:23:50.460 --> 00:23:52.990
Moon viewing season sure makes you want to eat <i>mochi</i>!

00:23:52.990 --> 00:23:54.200
Th-The kind pounded by moon rabbits?

00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:55.500
There can't be rabbits on the moon.

00:23:55.500 --> 00:23:58.970
Ah, Maia, you didn't know?
There's a Rabbit Empire on the moon!

00:23:58.970 --> 00:24:02.540
Preposterous! Rabbits can't live on the moon without air!

00:24:02.540 --> 00:24:03.970
It's supposed to be romantic! [<i>rouman</i>]

00:24:03.970 --> 00:24:05.610
--Are you nuts? [<i>maron</i>]
--Nuts are tasty, too.

00:24:05.610 --> 00:24:08.280
Episode 10: "Reach Them! My True Voice."

00:24:05.970 --> 00:24:08.480
"Episode 10: Reach Them! My True Voice"

00:24:08.280 --> 00:24:09.710
Let's go eat chestnut dumplings.
